The [#4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471) says "one issue, one fix queued". Its own table says
otherwise: two causes, and a note under them about reports where the date moves by one day.
The reports merged into #4471 are three problems, and each has its own ticket now.

Engineering has closed #4471: `parser` fixed, `hint` won't fix. Nothing in that update
touches the one-day move.

<Callout kind="warn">
The one-day move is still open. #4471 is closed, so issue 3 is the only open ticket for these
reports. Send new reports where the date moves by one day there, not to a parser ticket.
</Callout>

## The tickets

| problem | reports it covers | ticket | state |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `parser` | the `parser` row below | [issue 1](https://github.com/angeloocana/support-kb-4471-megadev/issues/1) | closed: fixed by `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales` |
| `hint` | the `hint` row below | [issue 2](https://github.com/angeloocana/support-kb-4471-megadev/issues/2) | closed: won't fix, the booking-v3 form is retired |
| `one-day move` | the one-day moves in the note under the table | [issue 3](https://github.com/angeloocana/support-kb-4471-megadev/issues/3) | **open** |

The counts are the desk's own view of #4471, as exported. It counts each report once, by id,
and files the one-day moves under `parser` by tenant. So issue 1 counts them too, but the parser
fix does not fix them.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## The three problems

### `parser`: the shared parser read dates month first

Our tenants write the day first, and the shared parser read every date month first. Day and
month swapped: "Booked for 2 December. The invite says 12 February." Every tenant on file had
it. **Fixed** by engineering: the parser now reads dd/mm for these locales.

### `hint`: booking-v3 told people to type the month first

The booking-v3 form printed `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People typed what the hint said,
month first, and the form read the date the tenant's way, day first. So the form itself swapped
day and month. Only booking-v3 tenants, and only bookings made through the form. The parser fix
did not touch this code. **Won't fix:** the booking-v3 form is retired, so no new reports should
come from it.

### `one-day move`: the date moves by one day, not by a month

Day and month do not swap here. The booking moves by one day: "Tuesday 6 October showed as
Monday." A client in Lisbon and a client in Toronto got different days for the same meeting.
This points at time-zone handling, not at the parser. The desk already read these reports
differently (`desk-notes.json`), but they stayed filed under `parser`. **Open:** find where a
booking's date crosses a time zone (invite, calendar, reminder).

## Why one ticket hid three

- [Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on the subject line. People
  write the same subjects ("Month and day swapped?", "Wrong day on the invite") for different
  bugs, so the subject cannot tell the bugs apart.
- Intake's tag is a guess from the reporter's browser. The cause depends on the tenant: its
  locale and its booking form. The "tagged as" column above shows how often the two disagree.
- The ticket export repeats some reports across pages. The table counts each report once, by id.

## What to do now

- **Engineering:** take issue 3. It is the only one of the three still open.
- **Desk:** merge a new report by its cause (tenant and the way the booking was made), not by
  its subject. A report where the date moves by one day goes to issue 3.
- **Decision 0001:** it is accepted, so nobody edits it. A new decision record should replace
  it with merging by cause.

